    "body": "Stacked on #2485. **All three PRs in this stack are meant to be merged together** \u2014 they are split for review only.\n\n## Summary\n\nDocumentation mode already renders `/`-separated slide names as nested breadcrumb dropdowns (`\"B2T2 / Table API / Constructors / vcat\"`). Tutorial mode has 25 lessons in one flat list. This PR names that hierarchy and then gives tutorial mode folders on top of it.\n\n### `SlidePath`\n\nThe hierarchy was an ad-hoc convention spread across three unrelated places: a local `split_filepath` plus inline `take`/`nth`/`dedup_f` in `EditorModeView.indicator_select`, ~60 hardcoded `\" / \"` literals in `src/b2t2/Slides.re` and `src/docslides/Slides.re`, and `\"Derivations / \" ++ spec.title` in `Init.re`.\n\n`src/web/util/SlidePath.re` makes it a type:\n\n```reason\ntype t = {\n  folders: list(string),\n  leaf: string,\n};\n```\n\nand owns the operations both modes need: `of_string`/`to_string`, `folder`/`same_folder`, the folder-scoped index arithmetic the navigation arrows use (`folder_indices`, `folder_position`, and `step_in_folder`, which clamps), and `breadcrumb` \u2014 the sibling-dropdown decomposition lifted out of the view.\n\n`indicator_select` is now a thin render over `breadcrumb` and takes `list(SlidePath.t)`, which dropped 69 lines from it along with two latent crashes it had been carrying:\n\n- `List.nth(parts', prefix_depth)` raised `Failure(\"nth\")` whenever one slide name was an exact proper prefix of another \u2014 a slide named `Tables` alongside `Tables / Tables` would have taken down the whole top bar. Such a path is now skipped, making it merely unreachable from the deeper dropdown.\n- `Option.get` on the changed option's index lookup.\n\nSlide names stay plain strings at the persistence boundary \u2014 they are IndexedDB keys (`\"doc:\" ++ name`) and `.hzt` `@title` text \u2014 so nothing about the stored format changes; callers convert at the view/navigation boundary.\n\n### Tutorial folders\n\nA lesson's `@title` is now a `SlidePath`, and both arrow surfaces \u2014 the in-slide prev/next pair and the top-bar arrows \u2014 **step within the current lesson's folder**, clamping at its edges, so the last lesson of a folder shows `Done! \ud83c\udf89` instead of a next arrow. Crossing folders goes through the folder dropdown. The slide heading shows just the leaf, since the breadcrumb above it already names the folder.\n\n| Folder | Lessons |\n|---|---|\n| `Basics` | 19 \u2014 Holes through Labeled Tuple Projection |\n| `Tuple Structural Operations` | 3 \u2014 Extension, Omission, List Conversions |\n| `Tables` | 6 \u2014 Tables, Table Column Projection, Rich Probes, and the three Gradebook tasks below |\n\nRich Probes sits under Tables because it is a rich probe *for* tables.\n\n### Three tasks recovered from `tables-study`\n\n`Tables` also picks up Gradebook Midterm Mean, Gradebook Overall Grade, and Gradebook Tidy Term \u2014 study tasks that had never been ported off the `tables-study` branch, where they were `Ta_*.ml` zipper dumps of 0.5\u20130.9 MB each. They keep their original ids, so they are the same lessons the study ran.\n\nThey were converted by adapting the dumps to the current types (the drift was two things per file: `selection` gained `anchor_caret`/`smart_rounded`, and `refractors` dropped `autos`/`sample_cursor` with `manuals` unchanged), compiling them in alongside `TaskRefDocs`, and running `./hazel tutorial-decode` \u2014 which also expanded each task's composed `TaskRefDocs` sections into a literal `@reference`. None of that scaffolding is in the tree.\n\nTwo content fixes on top of the decode: Midterm Mean's table held 20 literals like `85.000000`, and past six significant digits a slide falls onto the quadratic parser (slowness being the only symptom), so those are normalized to `85.0`; and its hidden tests did not round-trip, because an implicit `\u00bf` hole collapses to nothing before a `,` inside a labeled tuple, so those twelve are now the explicit `?` token.\n\nNot ported, deliberately: the two Bug Identification tasks, which depend on live typing; the 27 pre-placed probe refractors these three carried (`Triggers.refractor_seg_to_seg` only emits `^^probe(...)` for a refractor whose id is a term root in the current parse, and these ids came from the older grammar, so 26 of 27 dropped); and the study's `setting_overrides` condition flags and `?treatment` A/B ordering, none of which has a `.hzt` marker. The commit records what each task's flags were.\n\nAll three start as real tasks \u2014 a hole in Midterm Mean, an identity-stub `tidy_term` \u2014 so their hidden tests fail until solved.\n\nRecategorizing is safe: lesson identity is the `id=<uuid>` flag introduced in #2485, not the title, so moving a lesson between folders does not reset anyone's saved progress.\n\n`hazel-programs/tutorial/README.md` documents the authoring rules \u2014 one folder segment per lesson, no title a proper prefix of another, a folder's lessons contiguous in `src/tutorialslides/Slides.re`, and `Basics / Holes` first because it is the lesson a fresh profile opens on.\n\n## Deliberately not done\n\nA \u2714 on a folder's dropdown option when the whole folder is complete. It cannot be built from current data: `TutorialsMode.Update.calculate` evaluates only the current lesson and `TutorialMode.Model.persist` saves only zippers, so `all_tests_passed` is `false` for every non-current lesson \u2014 which is also why today's per-lesson \u2714 from `return_title` can only ever show for the lesson you are standing on. A real folder \u2714 needs persisted per-lesson completion, which is its own change.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `make dev` builds clean, no new warnings\n- [x] `make test-quick` \u2014 3501/3501\n- [x] `./hazel tutorial-verify` \u2014 28/28 slides round-trip cleanly\n- [x] `Test_SlidePath` (23 cases) \u2014 parsing, accessors, folder navigation, and breadcrumb, including the proper-prefix path that used to raise and an out-of-range index\n- [x] `Test_Tutorial` (7 cases) \u2014 ratchets the authored lessons: folder set and sizes (`Basics x19`, `Tuple Structural Operations x3`, `Tables x6`), contiguity, `Basics / Holes` first as the default lesson, no title a proper prefix of another, and that repeated next/prev traverses exactly one folder and then stops\n- [x] Documentation mode \u2014 `B2T2 / \u2026` breadcrumbs and `Derivations / \u2026` still render and switch slides\n- [x] Tutorial mode \u2014 opens on `Basics / Holes`; arrows walk one folder and stop at its ends; the dropdown crosses folders\n- [x] `./hazel analyze --warnings` reports nothing on all three ported tasks' starting programs\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
